1
00:00:08,320 --> 00:00:12,960
Brighten up the peace and try stepping away,
won't you?

2
00:00:23,180 --> 00:00:28,460
of that after-rain day when it
seemed someone was calling out.

3
00:00:29,900 --> 00:00:32,660
I walked while looking back.

4
00:00:32,660 --> 00:00:35,340
Holding hands with Ga-chan,

5
00:00:35,340 --> 00:00:42,460
that mysterious feeling I had back then.

6
00:00:43,160 --> 00:00:47,740
So, on the tiles of the arcade street,

7
00:00:47,740 --> 00:00:53,520
I tried walking only on the black ones.

8
00:00:55,920 --> 00:00:59,680
Everyone was a child once,

9
00:00:59,680 --> 00:01:01,820
but everyone has forgotten.

10
00:01:02,720 --> 00:01:09,120
Politicians with their self-important faces,
and aunties with blue eyeshadow too.

11
00:01:09,600 --> 00:01:14,700
Why don't you turn at that corner?

12
00:01:15,700 --> 00:01:19,900
You can meet everyone, everyone.

13
00:01:22,100 --> 00:01:27,820
Over there, there's Kame-ari.
Surely there's Kame-ari.

14
00:01:29,120 --> 00:01:33,020
Everyone, come on over to our town!

15
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:34,680
Thank you.

16
00:02:23,440 --> 00:02:25,600
Skilled video cameraman

17
00:02:28,720 --> 00:02:32,320
Quite a lot of money, huh

18
00:02:33,360 --> 00:02:34,880
Looking for a part-time job?

19
00:02:35,340 --> 00:02:37,880
You just got your paycheck last week,
didn't you?

20
00:02:38,480 --> 00:02:40,920
I blew through it all the same day.

21
00:02:42,280 --> 00:02:45,240
You can't live a joyful
life on salary alone.

22
00:02:45,640 --> 00:02:48,420
Some freeters make as much as 300,000 yen,
you know.

23
00:02:48,921 --> 00:02:52,600
I can't stand letting some guy
with no steady job make that much.

24
00:02:53,040 --> 00:02:55,160
Starting today,
I'm going to be a freeter too.

25
00:02:55,480 --> 00:02:57,260
Senpai, aren't you a civil servant?

26
00:02:57,820 --> 00:03:00,540
So I'll be a freeter while
still working as a civil servant.

27
00:03:01,040 --> 00:03:02,520
That'll double my income!

28
00:03:03,960 --> 00:03:07,360
8,000 yen an hour! This is it!

29
00:03:24,180 --> 00:03:25,440
Look at you,
grinning and swaying around like an idiot

30
00:03:25,900 --> 00:03:27,100
Next, next!

31
00:03:28,540 --> 00:03:29,760
Move, move, move, move!

32
00:03:34,040 --> 00:03:36,780
8,000 yen an hour,
no mistake about that, right?

33
00:03:36,780 --> 00:03:38,320
Yeah, of course.

34
00:03:40,320 --> 00:03:42,740
All right!

35
00:03:42,790 --> 00:03:45,260
First round passed.

36
00:03:45,260 --> 00:03:47,060
Straight on to the second round.

37
00:03:47,640 --> 00:03:48,460
Hey, Kiroko!

38
00:03:49,720 --> 00:03:51,680
Third round, score 100!

39
00:03:56,060 --> 00:03:57,420
So only four remain

40
00:03:57,420 --> 00:03:58,640
Good, you're hired.

41
00:03:59,220 --> 00:04:02,960
This time, the 30th anniversary
project for Dai-Tokyo TV

42
00:04:02,960 --> 00:04:04,900
has been taken on by our company.

43
00:04:05,400 --> 00:04:07,280
This is truly an honor.

44
00:04:07,280 --> 00:04:11,240
We really want to make this project, on
which the company's fortunes depend, a success.

45
00:04:11,640 --> 00:04:13,940
So what exactly are we supposed to do?

46
00:04:15,180 --> 00:04:17,300
Everyone's going on location tomorrow.

47
00:04:17,300 --> 00:04:19,940
There's me as director,
plus the cameraman and soundman.

48
00:04:19,940 --> 00:04:22,320
Then the assistant director,
that is, the AD.

49
00:04:24,180 --> 00:04:29,540
Now then, you two will be assisting the AD.
That is, A

50
00:04:29,540 --> 00:04:34,780
D... it sounds like DDT, doesn't it?

51
00:04:42,420 --> 00:04:49,720
Will the super idol take on that mountain where shooting stars glow?
It's a project that just piggybacks on idol popularity

52
00:04:51,920 --> 00:04:53,100
From here on, we walk.

53
00:04:55,240 --> 00:04:58,940
Are the four of us really going to
carry all this equipment up the mountain?

54
00:04:58,940 --> 00:05:01,000
This is going to take some serious stamina.

55
00:05:01,000 --> 00:05:04,900
If you two don't carry it, who will?

56
00:05:04,900 --> 00:05:07,840
We can't afford to waste
a single minute today.

57
00:05:07,840 --> 00:05:13,740
That president is famous in the industry as a survivor of the old-school,
hot-blooded TV men, you know.

58
00:05:13,740 --> 00:05:16,020
Don't zone out. It's a super hauling job.

59
00:05:16,020 --> 00:05:19,720
You'd better brace yourself, because you'll
be made to work three times what you're paid.

60
00:05:19,720 --> 00:05:22,740
As long as I get my part-time pay,
I've got no complaints.

61
00:05:27,320 --> 00:05:28,040
Well, well.

62
00:05:28,760 --> 00:05:31,380
Then, for the CD campaign,
let's go with that approach.

63
00:05:31,380 --> 00:05:33,420
Thank you for coming all this way.

64
00:05:33,880 --> 00:05:35,960
Please take good care of us today.

65
00:05:36,720 --> 00:05:37,080
Nice to meet you.

66
00:05:37,720 --> 00:05:39,680
Wow, the air feels so fresh here.

67
00:05:41,760 --> 00:05:42,880
Hikaru-chan.

68
00:05:46,720 --> 00:05:49,200
It's Nagareboshi Hikaru, Hikaru-chan!

69
00:05:50,440 --> 00:05:51,080
Nice to meet you.

70
00:05:52,300 --> 00:05:52,940
Nice to meet you.

71
00:05:52,940 --> 00:05:56,020
Yes, Nagareboshi Hikaru is fully motivated!

72
00:05:59,500 --> 00:06:00,660
Just a little more.

73
00:06:01,520 --> 00:06:03,100
Let's make a good show.

74
00:06:03,840 --> 00:06:04,160
Yes.

75
00:06:04,160 --> 00:06:07,380
Hey, Director, if you handle her so roughly,
Hikaru will break.

76
00:06:08,180 --> 00:06:09,240
Oops, my apologies.

77
00:06:10,180 --> 00:06:12,420
What are you spacing out for?
Get ready right away!

78
00:06:13,240 --> 00:06:16,940
First, we'll record her opening
line here at the start of the hike.

79
00:06:16,940 --> 00:06:21,960
Next, the camera will follow Hikaru
as she walks along the riverside.

80
00:06:21,960 --> 00:06:22,660
Yes.

81
00:06:25,320 --> 00:06:29,880
Did you just tell our Nagareboshi Hikaru to walk the mountain trail,
Director?

82
00:06:30,660 --> 00:06:33,900
Did you hear? She told a super idol to walk!

83
00:06:35,360 --> 00:06:39,340
This is a mountain program,
so you really have to walk.

84
00:06:39,340 --> 00:06:42,420
Nagareboshi Hikaru doesn't
walk more than five steps.

85
00:06:43,120 --> 00:06:44,300
Because

86
00:06:44,980 --> 00:06:47,140
first, she's an idol.

87
00:06:47,140 --> 00:06:51,040
Second, she's a top star with three or four
"super"s attached.

88
00:06:51,660 --> 00:06:52,820
Understand?

89
00:06:53,840 --> 00:06:56,900
But unfortunately,
cars can't get past this point either,

90
00:06:56,900 --> 00:06:59,420
so unless Hikaru walks,

91
00:06:59,420 --> 00:07:01,580
we can't move forward with filming.

92
00:07:02,960 --> 00:07:03,680
I see.

93
00:07:04,360 --> 00:07:05,940
Well then, there's nothing we can do.

94
00:07:06,500 --> 00:07:08,260
Come on, let's go home, Hikaru-chan.

95
00:07:08,260 --> 00:07:09,460
Hey, you.

96
00:07:09,460 --> 00:07:11,460
You're really going to quit the
show after coming all this way?

97
00:07:11,460 --> 00:07:12,440
No way.

98
00:07:12,880 --> 00:07:15,060
We'll just hand it back to
another production company.

99
00:07:15,060 --> 00:07:15,740
What did you say?!

100
00:07:16,740 --> 00:07:20,340
If you think you can get by in this industry with that attitude,
you're in for a surprise, you fool.

101
00:07:20,760 --> 00:07:23,140
Of course we can get by, can't we?

102
00:07:23,140 --> 00:07:25,580
That's the privilege of a popular idol.

103
00:07:26,000 --> 00:07:27,720
Switching production companies?

104
00:07:27,720 --> 00:07:29,800
What's going to happen to our part-time job?

105
00:07:30,920 --> 00:07:32,460
I'm not joking.

106
00:07:33,460 --> 00:07:34,360
I'm not giving it back.

107
00:07:34,360 --> 00:07:35,360
Please move aside.

108
00:07:35,360 --> 00:07:36,580
President!

109
00:07:36,720 --> 00:07:40,020
Saying Hikaru-chan walked is a ridiculous joke,
seriously.

110
00:07:40,420 --> 00:07:44,360
As long as Super Idol Nagareboshi Hikaru is standing there,
it's as good as having climbed it.

111
00:07:44,360 --> 00:07:48,900
In other words, it's the same as reaching
the summit of Everest with a single rice stalk.

112
00:07:50,660 --> 00:07:52,360
Thank you, thank you.

113
00:07:53,300 --> 00:07:55,020
Where's the president's helicopter?

114
00:07:55,820 --> 00:07:59,500
It's the helicopter to carry
Nagareboshi Hikaru up the mountain.

115
00:08:00,060 --> 00:08:04,180
If the show falls apart after getting this far,
all that's left is red ink, you know.

116
00:08:04,180 --> 00:08:05,620
Are you fine with that?

117
00:08:06,300 --> 00:08:06,660
That's...

118
00:08:06,660 --> 00:08:08,860
Wouldn't that mean bankruptcy?

119
00:08:11,160 --> 00:08:13,360
The helicopter will be arriving shortly.

120
00:08:13,360 --> 00:08:15,400
Calling us in for something like that now...

121
00:08:15,400 --> 00:08:18,360
Demanding idol Nagareboshi Hikaru shines.

122
00:08:18,360 --> 00:08:21,420
Fled the location on the day of filming?

123
00:08:21,420 --> 00:08:24,540
It's a juicy story that the
daytime talk shows will jump on.

124
00:08:25,160 --> 00:08:26,880
Mr. Nobridgio's idol...

125
00:08:26,880 --> 00:08:28,640
over a minor scandal,

126
00:08:28,640 --> 00:08:30,900
the story of being unable to make a comeback

127
00:08:30,900 --> 00:08:33,500
is a dime a dozen in this industry.

128
00:08:34,340 --> 00:08:35,740
Scary, scary.

129
00:08:37,740 --> 00:08:40,080
Ahahaha! Is that so! A helicopter

130
00:08:40,560 --> 00:08:43,640
Then, Soutoon, I wish the
president would hurry up and go too.

131
00:08:46,600 --> 00:08:48,600
They're waiting.
What a bunch of troublesome guys.

132
00:08:54,080 --> 00:08:54,999
Right then,

133
00:08:55,049 --> 00:08:58,280
the departure line for the title back,
take one!

134
00:08:58,760 --> 00:09:00,900
We're going to conquer the Japanese Alps!

135
00:09:02,660 --> 00:09:03,400
Okay, that's a wrap.

136
00:09:04,180 --> 00:09:05,180
Good work, everyone.

137
00:09:05,180 --> 00:09:07,100
That was wonderful, Hikaru-chan.

138
00:09:07,280 --> 00:09:07,600
Thank you.

139
00:09:08,140 --> 00:09:08,620
Come on, come on.

140
00:09:09,840 --> 00:09:11,440
Well then, we'll be waiting for you up top.

141
00:09:12,820 --> 00:09:15,420
Hey, hey,
carry this heavy equipment for us, will you?

142
00:09:18,080 --> 00:09:21,380
Damn it, let's go. Don't dawdle.

143
00:09:22,440 --> 00:09:24,440
Hurry up,
we have to get there before the helicopter.

144
00:09:24,680 --> 00:09:27,980
There's no way we'll beat
the helicopter there, Gakun.

145
00:09:29,240 --> 00:09:33,000
If you've got time to talk, then get moving.
That's what the 8,000-yen hourly wage is for.

146
00:09:39,780 --> 00:09:41,340
Two more kilometers, hang in there!

147
00:09:47,340 --> 00:09:49,400
I can't breathe... I can't go on.

148
00:09:49,400 --> 00:09:50,900
Ohara, pull yourself together!

149
00:09:52,700 --> 00:09:54,320
This is no ordinary part-time job.

150
00:09:54,720 --> 00:09:56,580
I'll carry that luggage for you.

151
00:09:56,580 --> 00:09:58,260
I'm counting on you.

152
00:09:58,800 --> 00:10:01,060
But you'll pay us the wages for both of us.

153
00:10:01,060 --> 00:10:02,040
Fine.

154
00:10:03,900 --> 00:10:07,020
Even so,
a hundred spare batteries is too many.

155
00:10:07,020 --> 00:10:11,480
Each one weighs 1.5 kilos,
so a hundred comes to 150 kilos!

156
00:10:11,840 --> 00:10:13,840
Without batteries, the camera won't run.

157
00:10:13,840 --> 00:10:15,280
There's no such thing as being too careful.

158
00:10:15,280 --> 00:10:16,480
You're being overly cautious.

159
00:10:19,760 --> 00:10:21,240
That guy's out too.

160
00:10:21,240 --> 00:10:22,780
Leave it to me.

161
00:10:24,500 --> 00:10:25,820
This is really heavy.

162
00:10:26,780 --> 00:10:28,920
But now the part-time
pay is for three people.

163
00:10:28,920 --> 00:10:31,040
That's 24,000 yen an hour.

164
00:10:32,240 --> 00:10:33,520
I'm done for too.

165
00:10:36,600 --> 00:10:39,400
In the end it's the director,
the cameraman, the sound man,

166
00:10:39,400 --> 00:10:40,780
and me. That makes four.

167
00:10:41,580 --> 00:10:43,900
Talk about a forced march

168
00:10:49,040 --> 00:10:52,980
Geez, they're slow.
Making a super-duper idol wait!

169
00:10:59,940 --> 00:11:02,320
You're really late.

170
00:11:02,320 --> 00:11:06,100
You took so long,
I was just about to head home.

171
00:11:13,260 --> 00:11:16,600
Here we'll film Hikaru-san
climbing this cliff.

172
00:11:16,600 --> 00:11:20,180
Of course, for safety, you'll be wearing the equipment,
but

173
00:11:20,620 --> 00:11:21,760
Climb the cliff?

174
00:11:22,980 --> 00:11:24,660
You don't mean an Ultra Idol would...

175
00:11:24,660 --> 00:11:26,560
Not walk, not climb.

176
00:11:26,560 --> 00:11:28,540
What on earth did you come here for?

177
00:11:28,540 --> 00:11:29,020
Boss!

178
00:11:29,020 --> 00:11:30,020
We're in the red.

179
00:11:30,020 --> 00:11:31,720
Pull back!

180
00:11:37,260 --> 00:11:39,180
Make your expression fiercer.

181
00:11:44,460 --> 00:11:45,340
Yes, OK!

182
00:11:46,300 --> 00:11:47,460
That was perfect.

183
00:11:48,220 --> 00:11:49,200
Sorry.

184
00:11:49,200 --> 00:11:50,620
Thank you for your hard work.

185
00:11:56,440 --> 00:11:59,720
If it's just this kind of shoot, we didn't
need to come all the way up the mountain.

186
00:11:59,720 --> 00:12:01,880
They could've just done the
special effects in a studio.

187
00:12:02,880 --> 00:12:04,300
I want to walk on my own.

188
00:12:05,180 --> 00:12:06,460
I want to walk.

189
00:12:07,060 --> 00:12:08,220
Even though I want to walk.

190
00:12:08,720 --> 00:12:11,180
What's the problem?
If you want to walk, then just walk!

191
00:12:13,480 --> 00:12:15,540
If you want to walk, then just walk.

192
00:12:16,300 --> 00:12:18,400
If you want to walk, then just walk.

193
00:12:23,700 --> 00:12:24,660
How about it?

194
00:12:26,100 --> 00:12:27,360
You should just walk.

195
00:12:28,680 --> 00:12:30,340
We're heading to the next point.

196
00:12:30,840 --> 00:12:32,880
Come on, you could at least give us a ride.

197
00:12:32,880 --> 00:12:41,480
Yasuza, you look pale. Are you okay?

198
00:12:42,180 --> 00:12:44,260
I've been pulling all-nighters lately.

199
00:12:45,780 --> 00:12:48,900
Pull yourself together!

200
00:12:48,900 --> 00:12:49,200
Hey!

201
00:12:49,300 --> 00:12:50,380
B-boring...

202
00:12:55,580 --> 00:12:57,260
What on earth are you thinking?

203
00:12:57,760 --> 00:13:00,240
This is way more of a documentary than that!

204
00:13:00,440 --> 00:13:01,280
Don't mess with me!

205
00:13:01,520 --> 00:13:02,400
You idiot!

206
00:13:20,740 --> 00:13:21,900
Okay, that's a wrap.

207
00:13:23,020 --> 00:13:24,120
Good work, everyone.

208
00:13:24,120 --> 00:13:27,720
In the end, it's just me and
the president left on the staff.

209
00:13:27,720 --> 00:13:32,060
No matter what we do,
Hikaru-chan is just so cute.

210
00:13:32,860 --> 00:13:36,540
But just climbing the
mountain isn't interesting.

211
00:13:38,860 --> 00:13:39,940
I've got it.

212
00:13:40,600 --> 00:13:42,260
A chick falls out of that nest.

213
00:13:42,260 --> 00:13:45,920
Shooting Star Hikaru saves it
and puts it back in the nest.

214
00:13:45,920 --> 00:13:49,700
It'll be a great scene that
shows off Hikaru-chan's kindness.

215
00:13:51,380 --> 00:13:54,920
If she won't climb or walk, how on
earth are we supposed to get this shot?

216
00:13:54,920 --> 00:13:56,760
After all, this is staged, isn't it?

217
00:13:56,760 --> 00:13:59,100
Are you saying we can't get it?

218
00:13:59,100 --> 00:14:00,320
Of course.

219
00:14:00,320 --> 00:14:02,060
Well then, there's no choice.

220
00:14:03,000 --> 00:14:04,360
Well, let's head back.

221
00:14:04,780 --> 00:14:05,740
Hold on a second.

222
00:14:06,600 --> 00:14:09,380
We're paying for five
people's part-time wages here.

223
00:14:10,200 --> 00:14:11,720
Words like "give up"

224
00:14:12,340 --> 00:14:14,940
should only be said
when you're dying, right?

225
00:14:17,960 --> 00:14:20,140
You only give up when you're dead.

226
00:14:27,400 --> 00:14:28,320
Let's go.

227
00:14:29,280 --> 00:14:33,000
The chick -

228
00:14:34,880 --> 00:14:35,300
Right.

229
00:14:42,460 --> 00:14:45,440
Well, it's a bit puffed up,
so it should still work.

230
00:14:47,020 --> 00:14:48,260
I'm borrowing this for a bit.

231
00:14:48,260 --> 00:14:50,800
I'll put it back right away.

232
00:14:56,180 --> 00:14:57,360
Stop that.

233
00:15:00,560 --> 00:15:02,760
40,000 yen an hour.

234
00:15:06,620 --> 00:15:07,400
Welcome back.

235
00:15:10,040 --> 00:15:11,080
Alright, okay.

236
00:15:11,680 --> 00:15:12,740
Put the nest back.

237
00:15:13,260 --> 00:15:14,420
Wonderful.

238
00:15:15,020 --> 00:15:16,500
Hikaru-chan, you're the best.

239
00:15:16,500 --> 00:15:20,160
Hikaru-chan's kindness
will bring fans to tears.

240
00:15:20,920 --> 00:15:22,400
With this, it's not just young people,

241
00:15:22,400 --> 00:15:25,200
we've totally won over
middle-aged and older audiences too.

242
00:15:25,780 --> 00:15:34,120
Wow, how beautiful.

243
00:15:35,540 --> 00:15:36,480
Okay, good.

244
00:15:36,480 --> 00:15:38,020
Good work, everyone.

245
00:15:40,460 --> 00:15:42,380
What berry is this?

246
00:15:42,860 --> 00:15:43,240
I don't know.

247
00:15:43,240 --> 00:15:44,420
They're pretty, aren't they?

248
00:15:44,960 --> 00:15:46,300
They're lingonberries.

249
00:15:46,300 --> 00:15:47,960
So that's it.

250
00:15:47,960 --> 00:15:48,860
Can you eat them?

251
00:15:48,860 --> 00:15:49,420
Yes.

252
00:15:54,180 --> 00:15:55,280
They're tasty.

253
00:15:56,140 --> 00:15:58,100
But you really know your stuff, don't you?

254
00:15:58,100 --> 00:16:03,060
Before my debut,
my father often took me up mountains.

255
00:16:04,120 --> 00:16:05,260
You don't look the type.

256
00:16:06,800 --> 00:16:07,580
I was quite the mountaineer, you know.

257
00:16:08,980 --> 00:16:10,280
Hahaha.

258
00:16:15,860 --> 00:16:16,920
Ohhhhhhhh!

259
00:16:19,660 --> 00:16:22,960
Great expression! Alright, let's shoot
the scene of eating the cowberries!

260
00:16:24,140 --> 00:16:24,460
Yes!

261
00:16:25,160 --> 00:16:29,100
Oh Hikaru,
you mustn't eat this sort of thing.

262
00:16:29,520 --> 00:16:31,020
But everyone is eating them.

263
00:16:31,240 --> 00:16:35,140
No, you mustn't. If you get an upset stomach,
it'll affect tomorrow's work, won't it?

264
00:16:37,300 --> 00:16:42,740
If Nagareboshi Hikaru misses even one episode,
the show will lose tens of millions in revenue.

265
00:16:42,740 --> 00:16:44,840
Will you take responsibility for that?

266
00:16:45,100 --> 00:16:46,280
Tens of millions.

267
00:16:46,980 --> 00:16:49,200
Then let's shoot the eating part separately.

268
00:16:52,740 --> 00:16:54,000
Alright, that's enough.

269
00:16:54,000 --> 00:16:56,380
Somehow it just isn't working.

270
00:16:57,380 --> 00:17:00,720
As expected, wild plants like
these just don't suit Hikaru.

271
00:17:00,720 --> 00:17:02,080
Let's stop.

272
00:17:04,940 --> 00:17:06,720
Hikaru, let's move on to the next spot.

273
00:17:17,140 --> 00:17:21,460
We're planning to shoot
Hikaru's swimming scene here,

274
00:17:28,140 --> 00:17:31,100
but what exactly are we
going to use this footage for?

275
00:17:32,080 --> 00:17:35,600
We'll film Shooting Star Hikaru swimming
in a pool later and composite it in.

276
00:17:36,160 --> 00:17:36,560
I see.

277
00:17:38,040 --> 00:17:39,980
Hey, the water's a bit too shallow.

278
00:17:39,980 --> 00:17:42,280
Wait, the screen's...

279
00:17:42,280 --> 00:17:44,820
The cameraman's sinking!

280
00:17:49,940 --> 00:17:51,300
You idiot!

281
00:17:51,300 --> 00:17:52,780
Are you trying to turn this into a puddle?

282
00:17:52,780 --> 00:17:53,580
Be careful!

283
00:17:55,600 --> 00:17:56,240
A rock!

284
00:17:56,800 --> 00:17:57,560
Hit it!

285
00:17:59,180 --> 00:17:59,980
Whoa!

286
00:17:59,980 --> 00:18:01,260
Such a... hidden...

287
00:18:01,260 --> 00:18:02,160
Shut up!

288
00:18:03,360 --> 00:18:03,960
Tsu -

289
00:18:04,860 --> 00:18:06,160
It's not the temple's money, you know.

290
00:18:06,160 --> 00:18:07,260
You got fat, you bastard!

291
00:18:07,800 --> 00:18:09,220
Sorry, sorry.

292
00:18:09,220 --> 00:18:12,880
But just swimming isn't
very interesting, is it?

293
00:18:13,320 --> 00:18:14,300
Something like...

294
00:18:15,360 --> 00:18:16,160
That's right.

295
00:18:16,960 --> 00:18:19,780
How about having her jump from
that rock into the waterfall pool?

296
00:18:20,900 --> 00:18:23,400
That'll make for some thrilling footage.

297
00:18:23,400 --> 00:18:25,780
Fans will be on the edge
of their seats, I bet.

298
00:18:27,040 --> 00:18:28,500
I can't take it anymore.

299
00:18:29,980 --> 00:18:32,280
You're not going to have her jump, right?
Of course not.

300
00:18:32,900 --> 00:18:39,140
This show is billed as a documentary, you know!
How is a place full of staged scenes and cheap tricks like this a documentary?

301
00:18:39,140 --> 00:18:45,160
Come on. Whether it's staged or directed,
all that matters is moving the viewers.

302
00:18:46,060 --> 00:18:54,380
No, it's the raw, real footage that moves people more deeply.
Viewers are waiting for Idol Shooting Star Hikaru.

303
00:18:54,960 --> 00:18:58,920
Nobody wants the unfiltered
Shooting Star Hikaru.

304
00:18:59,520 --> 00:19:03,840
The Shooting Star Hikaru we create, the
constructed image, is the real Shooting Star Hikaru.

305
00:19:05,500 --> 00:19:08,780
After all, she's an idol,
a constructed image through and through.

306
00:19:16,740 --> 00:19:18,060
Alright, OK, that's it for here.

307
00:19:30,840 --> 00:19:34,020
Let's save the line about
giving up for when you're dying.

308
00:19:35,200 --> 00:19:36,380
I can do it too.

309
00:19:36,860 --> 00:19:38,500
I can do it too!

310
00:19:47,860 --> 00:19:50,060
No matter how much you drink,
it's still only half full.

311
00:19:50,060 --> 00:19:51,180
Hey, Hikaru-chan.

312
00:19:52,020 --> 00:19:53,020
I'll swim.

313
00:19:53,480 --> 00:19:54,800
Did you say something?

314
00:19:55,840 --> 00:19:56,600
Hikaru-chan?

315
00:19:57,040 --> 00:19:58,900
I'll swim.

316
00:19:59,680 --> 00:20:01,160
What's wrong, Hikaru-chan?

317
00:20:01,160 --> 00:20:03,360
I can do it too.

318
00:20:03,360 --> 00:20:05,380
I'm not a doll.

319
00:20:18,260 --> 00:20:20,220
Hey, hey, Hikaru-chan!

320
00:20:23,300 --> 00:20:24,500
Hikaru.

321
00:20:25,440 --> 00:20:25,980
This is...!

322
00:20:32,120 --> 00:20:33,760
Aaaaaah!

323
00:20:37,960 --> 00:20:39,920
Hikaru-chan.

324
00:20:59,320 --> 00:21:02,120
Hikaru-chan

325
00:21:08,940 --> 00:21:10,040
Hikaru!

326
00:21:13,040 --> 00:21:14,840
This feels so good.

327
00:21:17,780 --> 00:21:20,680
I'd forgotten this feeling for so long.

328
00:21:24,280 --> 00:21:26,800
I'm quitting the entertainment world,
of all things.

329
00:21:27,380 --> 00:21:31,640
From now on, I'll walk the path I believe in,
on my own two feet.

330
00:21:31,640 --> 00:21:34,100
Why all of a sudden?

331
00:21:34,560 --> 00:21:36,940
Ryo-san taught me that.

332
00:21:36,940 --> 00:21:37,540
What?

333
00:21:38,200 --> 00:21:40,820
Thank you for waking me up.

334
00:21:40,820 --> 00:21:42,540
Ugh, as for me...

335
00:21:42,540 --> 00:21:45,780
Is this your doing?
What did you do to Hikaru?

336
00:21:45,780 --> 00:21:47,460
What did you put into Hikaru's head?

337
00:21:47,460 --> 00:21:49,540
No, I don't know anything about it.

338
00:21:49,540 --> 00:21:51,540
And I have one request.

339
00:21:52,240 --> 00:21:55,280
Please stop broadcasting this video.

340
00:21:56,020 --> 00:21:59,560
That wasn't the real me. It was all lies.

341
00:22:01,360 --> 00:22:02,580
You've got to be kidding.

342
00:22:02,580 --> 00:22:05,680
Oh no, if she really retires...

343
00:22:05,680 --> 00:22:07,600
Isn't this her last job?

344
00:22:08,160 --> 00:22:11,800
We can't possibly shelve
such valuable footage.

345
00:22:11,800 --> 00:22:13,300
Valuable footage

346
00:22:13,300 --> 00:22:18,040
Mr. President,
please keep that tape under strict guard.

347
00:22:18,040 --> 00:22:22,020
Don't worry, I won't let anyone touch it.

348
00:22:25,860 --> 00:22:29,160
I'm sorry, Mr. President, because of me...

349
00:22:29,560 --> 00:22:31,695
No, it's I who should be thanking you.

350
00:22:31,745 --> 00:22:35,180
Thanks to you, I've come to my senses too.
Thank you.

351
00:22:35,960 --> 00:22:38,940
Hold on! What about my part-time pay, then?

352
00:22:39,540 --> 00:22:43,080
Our company is going bankrupt now.
Sorry, but I can't pay your part-time wages.

353
00:22:43,420 --> 00:22:48,060
What?! After all that hard work,
it was 40,000 yen an hour?!

354
00:22:48,500 --> 00:22:49,640
This is all your fault!

355
00:22:51,080 --> 00:22:53,320
What are you going to do about this?
I'll sue you!

356
00:22:54,020 --> 00:22:56,020
I don't know! I'm a victim too!

357
00:22:58,080 --> 00:23:01,840
Senpai, you did it again,
Nagareboshi Kōtaku.

358
00:23:01,840 --> 00:23:05,480
Now what, Everest or the Matterhorn?

359
00:23:05,480 --> 00:23:07,880
Did you go solo up the Amazon River?

360
00:23:07,880 --> 00:23:12,560
A solo crossing of Antarctica, they say?
Wow, that's amazing.

361
00:23:13,440 --> 00:23:16,960
You're leaving the entertainment world to become an adventurer,
after all.

362
00:23:17,560 --> 00:23:18,700
We were really surprised.

363
00:23:18,700 --> 00:23:21,480
Because of that,
I turned all of Japan's fans against me

364
00:23:21,480 --> 00:23:23,040
and I went through hell for it!

365
00:23:23,540 --> 00:23:28,480
I told you to walk on your own two feet, but
I never said to walk all the way to Antarctica!

366
00:23:30,800 --> 00:23:33,740
I have finally reached
the bottom of Antarctica.

367
00:23:34,340 --> 00:23:36,860
It's as if yesterday's
blizzard never happened.

368
00:23:36,860 --> 00:23:39,660
Hikaru, get a little closer to the penguins.

369
00:23:40,180 --> 00:23:41,200
You idiot!

370
00:23:41,740 --> 00:23:44,800
Capturing things as they are,
that's what a documentary is.

371
00:23:45,160 --> 00:23:47,180
Thank you all for supporting me.

372
00:23:48,220 --> 00:23:52,260
And the reason I am who I
am now is that you taught me

373
00:23:53,040 --> 00:23:54,080
to walk on my own two feet.
It's thanks to the staff.

374
00:23:55,480 --> 00:23:56,740
Thank you, Kankichi Ryotsu-san.

375
00:24:23,040 --> 00:24:25,700
Unreasonable demands are only natural

376
00:24:26,940 --> 00:24:30,540
But I play it cool with one hand

377
00:24:30,540 --> 00:24:33,340
Beef bowl, cloudy with extra sauce

378
00:24:33,340 --> 00:24:36,600
The irritation of endless overtime

379
00:24:36,600 --> 00:24:40,220
Clears right up with a bit of irritation

380
00:24:43,520 --> 00:24:46,040
Every day is no problem

381
00:24:46,040 --> 00:24:49,980
After passing through a hot shower

382
00:24:49,980 --> 00:24:56,600
Every day's no-problem-brain,
my energy restored by a sleep pillow

383
00:24:59,700 --> 00:25:06,220
Every day's no-problem-brain,
I love a girl like me

384
00:25:06,220 --> 00:25:13,020
Every day's no-problem-brain,
hearts flying on Monday

385
00:25:13,020 --> 00:25:17,180
Monday, Monday, no-problem-brain

386
00:25:21,540 --> 00:25:23,520
In the rice naming contest

387
00:25:23,520 --> 00:25:26,100
The rice name I came up with,
Komecchauna, won first place

388
00:25:26,100 --> 00:25:28,220
They sent me so much rice I nearly died

389
00:25:28,820 --> 00:25:30,640
But I can't possibly eat it all by myself

390
00:25:30,640 --> 00:25:33,620
That's it, I'll use this as
capital and start a business

391
00:25:33,620 --> 00:25:37,100
Next time, the departure of
rice and rice balls, see you then

